                            <p></p><h3>Definition of "model-2900":</h3><p><b>Model 2900</b> is the name of a rectangular condenser microphone capsule developed by Swedish mic manufacturer Milab.</p><p>The Model 2900 is a revision of the Model 2700; both are rectangular capsules using polyester diaphragms metallized with aluminum. </p><p>The Model 2900 was developed in 2000. It delivered two benefits over the older design:</p><ol style="margin-left: 3em"><li>Improved frequency response.</li><li>Lower self-noise.</li></ol><p><img src="/images/mic_extras/milab/model_2700_capsule.jpg" width="100" class="thumb shaft" alt="Milab Model 2700 capsule" /><br />According to Milab, the two capsules cannot be distinguished visually. </p><p>The Model 2900 capsule (like the Model 2700) measures 36mm x 19mm.</p>
